    {
      "who": "MIA",
      "text": "Whales breathe air, just like us! They're mammals, not fish.",
      "punch": "air",
      "board": {
        "type": "big",
        "icon": "🐋",
        "text": "Whales breathe air!",
        "cue": "air",
        "sub": "Mammals, not fish",
        "sub_cue": "mammals"
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "LEO",
      "text": "Then how do they get air in the ocean?"
    },
    {
      "who": "MIA",
      "text": "They swim up and breathe through a blowhole. It's like a nose on top of their head!",
      "board": {
        "type": "big",
        "icon": "🐳",
        "text": "The blowhole",
        "cue": "blowhole",
        "sub": "A nose on top!",
        "sub_cue": "nose"
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "LEO",
      "text": "Why is it on top?"
    },
    {
      "who": "MIA",
      "text": "So they don't have to lift their whole head out. They just pop up, take a breath, and dive back down.",
      "board": {
        "type": "cycle",
        "title": "Up and down",
        "center": "🐋",
        "items": [
          {
            "icon": "⬆️",
            "label": "Pop up",
            "cue": "pop"
          },
          {
            "icon": "💨",
            "label": "Take a breath",
            "cue": "breath"
          },
          {
            "icon": "⬇️",
            "label": "Dive down",
            "cue": "dive"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "LEO",
      "text": "What's that big spray I see in pictures?"
    },
    {
      "who": "MIA",
      "text": "That's called a blow! It's mostly warm breath turning into a misty cloud.",
      "board": {
        "type": "big",
        "icon": "☁️",
        "text": "The blow",
        "cue": "blow",
        "sub": "Warm, misty breath",
        "sub_cue": "misty"
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "LEO",
      "text": "How long can a whale hold its breath?"
    },
    {
      "who": "MIA",
      "text": "Some big whales can stay underwater for more than an hour! Others come up more often.",
      "punch": "hour",
      "board": {
        "type": "big",
        "icon": "⏱️",
        "text": "More than an hour!",
        "cue": "hour",
        "sub": "Others come up often",
        "sub_cue": "others"
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "LEO",
      "text": "Wow! Do baby whales know how to breathe?"
    },
    {
      "who": "MIA",
      "text": "When a baby whale is born, its mum often helps it up for its very first breath.",
      "board": {
        "type": "big",
        "icon": "🐳",
        "text": "First breath!",
        "cue": "first",
        "sub": "Mum helps it up",
        "sub_cue": "mum"
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "LEO",
      "text": "So whales breathe air through a blowhole on top of their head!",
